Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Organization: Me organized? Not here!
Newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.osf1,comp.unix.osf.misc


Hi folks.

I have setup DNS for testing. I have two machines, a DNS server and a
DNS client. I would like to setup mail so I can address on my domen.

Configuration:
--------------

Domain:		ev
DNS Server:	Quark.ev = 192.168.5.204
DNS Client:	DuleD.ev = 192.168.63.16

Mail-Hub:	Quark.ev

DNS is working properly.
Furthermore, when I start "nslookup", set qtype=MX and type "ev", I get
Quark.ev (just as it should).

I have an alias on Quark.ev: "Nikola.Milutinovic: nikola".

This all works:
	mail nikola@Quark.ev
	mail Nikola>milutinovic@Quark.ev
and delivers mail to nikola@Quark.ev

I have setup both machines via "mailsetup" utility, the way it seamed
appropriate.

Problem:
--------

When I try either of these:
	mail nikola@ev
	mail Nikola.Milutinovic@ev
I get bounced from my (client at DuleD) machine. The transcript of the
session is something like this:

421 Deferred ev.ev ... Not owner
550 nikola@ev no such host (authoritative answer from name server): Not
owner.

Now, I'm stuck. I wouldn't wan't to start digging in sendmail.cf if I
don't have to.

Any help would be appreciated.

Nix.




