Steinar Haug <sthaug@nethelp.no> wrote:
>
>On the system where I'm typing this, you can only login directly to root
>on the physical console. None of the methods you mentioned here work, for
>good reasons.

If you can lock out all the other methods then, yes, I agree that it
could be useful.  I should be interested (seriously) to know which
version of OSF/1 has enough control to do that.  I did actually try to
restrict root login, and gave up when I found that I couldn't block
most of the cases that were likely to be used by a hacker, but could
make life more difficult for myself :-(

Yes, I know that you can do it if you lock out rlogin, telnet, rexec
and xdm entirely, but that makes a system pretty hard to use in most
environments.  Similarly, replacing all of those with customised
versions make a system rather unlike OSF/1.  Login itself can be
controlled by the privileged terminal facility, but most systems nowadays
don't run getty to anything EXCEPT the console!


