Danno wrote:
> 
> Digital UNIX 4.0b
> 
> can I delete (or move)  /genvmunix ???
> 
> its' about 8 megs and I could use the space
> 
> (assuming vmunix is my boot kernel image)...
Certainly. genvmunix is intended to be the backup kernel. Deleting it is
kind of like painting yourself into the corner. It is a good practice to
have a known good kernel in your root file system as a backup in the
event something happens to your boot kernel. If you do blow it away,
make sure that you have a way to boot in the event your boot kernel gets
blown. While it is a pain, you could always boot from another hard disk,
CDROM, or RIS, and restore the genvmunix in a pinch. 
