Not from me ,but got it some time ago in this news group, works well, I did
it several times. :

 From: schroedj@ub.uni-marburg.de (Juergen Schroeder)

The lack of filtering by printing remote is usual in most unix (lpd) types.
This can't be elegant overided by a old but not well known trick:

make a printqueue which print raw to the remote printer

make multiple printqueues for the features you want have
eg one called landscape

this should have this entries in the printcap:
        :if=/usr/local/daemon/filter/input_filter_landscape:\
        :lp=/dev/null:\

make the filter input_filter_landscape

(echo "here the esc-sequences for initialising the printer & landscape mode"

 cat - ) | lpr -Praw

thats all
you can make this queues if you want on only one machine and print remote
to this machine.

No fiddeling with lpd source code.


