You certainly can mount the root and usr file systems from the 4.0D on
the 4.0B system. I used to do that all the time with different base
levels of 5.0. (for testing Kernels and libc). You cannot simply mount
the 4.0D root as your 4.0B root. However, there are some changes on 4.0D
which may render some 4.0D binaries unusable on 4.0B. Digital goes to
great lengths to preserve binary compatibility so all of your 4.0B
binaries should run on 4.0D. 
