First of all, find out if your machine can see the tape (a standard
tape, BTW, I have it on several machines). From firmware console (halted
state) type:

>>> sh dev
Polling NCR
......................................
mka6.0.0.1.0	MKa600		TLZ09
......................................

You should see the tape (something like that above).

Then make sure your kernel has been informed of it (built when the tape
was in the machine), see file /sys/conf/<HOST_NAME_IN_CAPS>, I think (it
was on 3.2G).

Then you can do:

# cd /dev
# ./MAKEDEV tz6

